# What stays OUT of the self-hosting image (beta 10693). Everything else in
# the tree is served as-is: index.html, js/, css/, assets/, vendor/, the
# baselines, the scripts and the templates — exactly what GitHub Pages serves.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
CLAUDE.md
package.json
package-lock.json
node_modules
tests
docs
_to_delete
Claude outputs

# A tenant-specific auth override belongs to the machine it was written on,
# never to an image somebody else might pull.
js/authConfig.local.js

# The local-only folders a build from ~/REPO/TUNO would otherwise copy in:
# customer brandings (never published from this repo) and the Terraform
# deployment (its own repo, pushed to Azure Repos). All gitignored, but
# .dockerignore reads the working tree, not the index.
pvm
dovilo
cloudfellows
terraform

# The deploy scaffolding: run by the operator, not served to a browser.
selfhost/install.sh
selfhost/install.ps1
selfhost/docker-compose.yml
selfhost/resolve-digest.sh
selfhost/check-headers.py
# NOT selfhost/nginx.conf or selfhost/docker-entrypoint.sh - the Dockerfile
# COPYs both, so excluding them here would break the build rather than slim
# the image. The web-root copy of the entrypoint is removed in the Dockerfile.
